    "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::http-request-duplication::a57c178b": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::http-request-duplication::a57c178b",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "temper_request and temper_governance_request are nearly identical functions with duplicated response handling logic",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "low_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-sandbox/src/http.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "temper_request (lines 13-63) and temper_governance_request (lines 66-113) share identical response body parsing, empty-body handling, authz denied formatting, and error formatting logic. temper_request_bytes (lines 116-158) also duplicates the response parsing. The only differences are in header construction (principal kind and default principal ID)."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract a shared response-processing helper (e.g. parse_temper_response) and a request-builder that accepts a header configuration enum or struct. Each public function would configure headers then delegate to the shared core.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Disappeared from scan \u2014 likely fixed",
      "first_seen": "2026-03-05T17:18:48+00:00",
