    "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::wide-param-dispatch-blocking::00a01594": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::wide-param-dispatch-blocking::00a01594",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "BlockingWasmDispatch struct is a thin wrapper that immediately destructures into 8 positional arguments",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "abstraction_fitness",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/state/dispatch_blocking.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "BlockingWasmDispatch (lines 13-22) wraps 8 borrowed fields. dispatch_wasm_integrations_blocking (lines 31-51) immediately destructures it into positional arguments passed to dispatch_wasm_integrations_internal. The struct exists only to satisfy the too_many_arguments clippy lint rather than adding genuine domain encapsulation. The internal method still takes 9 positional parameters."
        ],
        "suggestion": "If the struct is kept, have dispatch_wasm_integrations_internal accept it directly instead of destructuring back to positional args. Alternatively, define a shared WasmDispatchRequest that both blocking and non-blocking paths use natively.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
