    "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::observe-fallback-silent-degradation::7fcdd9dd": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::observe-fallback-silent-degradation::7fcdd9dd",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Observe endpoints silently degrade to empty responses when Turso is unavailable, with no indication to the caller",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "contract_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/agents.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "In list_agents (lines 81-119), if turso_opt() returns None or the query fails, the endpoint returns {agents: [], total: 0} with HTTP 200. The caller receives the same response shape whether no agents exist or the backend is unavailable. The tracing::warn on failure (line 110) is only visible in server logs. The same pattern occurs in list_evolution_records (lines 19-81), list_evolution_insights (lines 85-128), and handle_feature_requests."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Add a metadata field to fallback responses indicating data_source: 'unavailable' or return HTTP 503 when the backing store is not configured. Alternatively, include a boolean field like 'data_available': false in the fallback path.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Fixed despite wontfix \u2014 disappeared from scan (was wontfix)",
