          "dimension": "incomplete_migration",
          "related_files": [
            "crates/temper-server/src/odata/common.rs"
          ],
          "evidence": [
            "resolve_entity_type (line 62-73) first queries registry.resolve_entity_type(), then falls back to state.entity_set_map. tenant_csdl_xml (line 78-86) falls back to state.csdl_xml. tenant_entity_sets (line 91-98) falls back to state.entity_set_map. These legacy fields on ServerState represent the pre-multi-tenant architecture. The fallbacks are always-present code paths that may mask registry configuration issues."
          ],
          "suggestion": "If all production deployments now use the SpecRegistry, remove the legacy fallbacks and the corresponding fields from ServerState. If backward compatibility is still needed, add deprecation warnings when fallback paths are hit to track migration progress.",
