    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::read_endpoint_has_write_side_effects::6f867ab0": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::read_endpoint_has_write_side_effects::6f867ab0",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Feature-request listing endpoint mutates persistent/domain state on every read call",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/operations.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/insight_generator.rs",
          "crates/temper-store-turso/src/store.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`handle_feature_requests` (`operations.rs` lines ~219-267) generates feature requests, upserts them, and dispatches `CreateFeatureRequest` actions before returning list data.",
          "`generate_feature_requests` creates new `RecordHeader` IDs (`insight_generator.rs` lines ~387-390), so repeated GET requests produce new IDs and fresh inserts.",
          "`feature_requests.id` is the primary key (`schema.rs` line ~189) and upsert conflict key (`store.rs` lines ~567-571), so changing IDs bypass deduplication."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Split this into explicit command/query seams: move generation/upsert/entity-creation to a scheduled job or POST endpoint, and keep GET as pure read from persisted projections keyed by a stable dedup key.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
