      "summary": "Postgres and Turso registry restore paths duplicate orchestration logic.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`load_registry_from_postgres` and `load_registry_from_turso` repeat the same steps (group rows by tenant, parse CSDL, build IOA pairs, register tenant, set verification statuses) across `crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs:212-369`.",
          "Because evolution reads are already backend-split in server routes (`records_list.rs` Turso-only), this duplicate restore orchestration compounds boundary divergence risk instead of centralizing backend differences."
