      "summary": "Missing identity headers default to System principal and bypass Cedar checks",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "authorization_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-authz/src/context.rs",
          "crates/temper-authz/src/engine.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/state/entity_ops.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`SecurityContext::from_headers` initializes `kind` as `PrincipalKind::System` (`context.rs:53`).",
          "`AuthzEngine::authorize_or_bypass` allows all `System` principals (`engine.rs:225-226`).",
          "Server authorization paths use `authorize_or_bypass` (`entity_ops.rs:267`), so absent/invalid headers can become allow-all."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Change default principal kind for missing/unknown headers to a non-bypass identity (e.g., `Anonymous`/`Customer`/`Agent` with deny-by-default), and reserve `System` only for explicitly trusted internal construction paths (e.g., `SecurityContext::system()`).",
