    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::duplicated_backend_restore_pipeline::d44bdcae": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::duplicated_backend_restore_pipeline::d44bdcae",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Postgres and Turso spec restore/upsert pipelines are duplicated instead of sharing a storage-boundary abstraction.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`load_registry_from_postgres` and `load_registry_from_turso` repeat the same grouping, CSDL parse, tenant registration, and verification-status restoration flow (`storage.rs` lines 212-293 vs 296-369).",
          "`upsert_loaded_specs_to_postgres` and `upsert_loaded_specs_to_turso` perform equivalent write semantics with separate codepaths (`storage.rs` lines 77-127 vs 472-499).",
          "The server side already has endpoint logic directly bound to one backend (`records_list.rs` lines 23-27, 89-90), increasing risk that backend behavior drifts across modules."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce a storage-port trait (e.g., `SpecPersistence`) that exposes normalized read/write operations and tenant-constraint access; implement Postgres/Turso adapters behind it, then keep one shared restore/upsert orchestration path.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
