    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::observe_layer_persistence_leak::56e8bdb0": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::observe_layer_persistence_leak::56e8bdb0",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "HTTP observe handlers depend directly on persistence-row shape and backend availability, leaking storage concerns into API boundary code.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs",
          "crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`list_evolution_records` and `list_evolution_insights` call Turso methods directly and manually decode/merge `r.data` JSON fields (`records_list.rs` lines 24-27, 44-49, 90-104).",
          "If Turso is absent or query fails, handlers emit empty success payloads (`records_list.rs` lines 72-80, 123-127), coupling API semantics to backend configuration state.",
          "A separate module already centralizes backend duality for related spec persistence (`storage.rs` lines 39-58, 296-369), but observe endpoints bypass such indirection."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move record retrieval and response-shaping into a domain service/repository that returns typed DTOs independent of Turso row internals; make handlers consume that service and surface explicit availability/errors instead of silent empty fallbacks.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
