    "review::.::holistic::package_organization::server_api_root_overloaded::bcfab25a": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::package_organization::server_api_root_overloaded::bcfab25a",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Root `api.rs` is a cross-domain sink and obscures ownership boundaries.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "package_organization",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/api.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`crates/temper-server/src/api.rs` is 1281 LOC and contains secrets, policy decisions, audit, authorize, REPL, and SSE handlers in one file.",
          "In `build_api_router`, routes under `/api` directly call `crate::observe::specs::*`, `crate::observe::wasm::*`, and `crate::observe::evolution::*`, so route ownership is split across root and observe modules."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Staged reorg plan: (1) Create `crates/temper-server/src/api/` with domain files (`secrets.rs`, `policies.rs`, `decisions.rs`, `authz.rs`, `repl.rs`) and keep `api/mod.rs` as router composition only. (2) Move observe-owned mutation handlers to `crates/temper-server/src/observe/management/` and expose a narrow routing API from observe, then have `api/mod.rs` call that API instead of direct function paths. (3) Update imports via `rg -n \"crate::observe::|handle_\" crates/temper-server/src/api* crates/temper-server/src/observe` and apply `cargo fmt`. (4) Validate with `cargo check -p temper-server` and `cargo test -p temper-server`.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
