    "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::backend_mirror_logic_in_cli_storage::fc255d8d": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::backend_mirror_logic_in_cli_storage::fc255d8d",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Backend-specific mirror flows duplicate the same domain restore/upsert workflow.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "high_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`load_registry_from_postgres` and `load_registry_from_turso` repeat the same grouping, CSDL parse, tenant registration, and status restoration algorithm with backend-specific row retrieval (storage.rs lines 212-294 and 297-369).",
          "`upsert_loaded_specs_to_postgres` and `upsert_loaded_specs_to_turso` duplicate tenant/spec upsert semantics in two codepaths (lines 77-128 and 473-499), increasing drift risk whenever persistence rules change.",
          "`records_list.rs` reaches directly into Turso from handler methods (lines 24-27, 89-90), reinforcing backend-specific coupling at call sites instead of through a unified domain repository."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce a backend-agnostic repository trait (or adapter layer) for spec restore/upsert/evolution queries and centralize the domain algorithm once; backend adapters should only implement row fetch/store primitives.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
