    "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::docs_runtime_storage_contract_drift::0b81244b": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::docs_runtime_storage_contract_drift::0b81244b",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Evolution API contract says multi-backend, runtime exposes Turso-only reads with silent empty fallback",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "high_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "README.md",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs",
          "crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "README advertises persistence as \"Postgres or Turso/libSQL\" and marks Evolution Engine as done (README.md:41, README.md:166, README.md:216, README.md:219).",
          "Observe handlers hardcode Turso semantics (\"single source of truth\") and return HTTP 200 empty payload when backend is absent/fails (crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/records_list.rs:23-24, :67-80, :88-89, :118-127).",
          "CLI storage bootstrap still creates/migrates Postgres evolution records store (crates/temper-cli/src/serve/storage.rs:49-54), showing backend capability exists but is not reflected in observe contracts."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Define one canonical evolution-read contract at the server boundary (trait/service) that supports both Postgres and Turso, and make observe handlers depend on it; if a backend is intentionally unsupported, explicitly document and return a typed error instead of empty success.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
