      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Tool execution API uses two error channels, increasing branch complexity and inconsistency.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "low_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-agent-runtime/src/tools/mod.rs",
          "crates/temper-mcp/src/error.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`crates/temper-agent-runtime/src/tools/mod.rs:27-32` defines `ToolResult::{Success, Error}`.",
          "`crates/temper-agent-runtime/src/tools/mod.rs:55` also returns `anyhow::Result<ToolResult>`, so failures can be `Err(_)` or `Ok(ToolResult::Error(_))`.",
          "`crates/temper-mcp/src/error.rs` shows a typed single-channel approach (`McpResult<T>`) already used elsewhere."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Collapse to one failure channel: return `Result<ToolOutput, ToolError>` (typed enum) and remove `ToolResult::Error`, so callers handle errors in one predictable path.",
