          "crates/temper-mcp/src/error.rs",
          "crates/temper-agent-runtime/src/tools/mod.rs",
          "crates/temper-observe/src/error.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`crates/temper-mcp/src/error.rs:3-6` states the crate moved to a unified typed `McpError`, but variants like `Transport(String)`, `Tool(String)`, `Runtime(String)`, `Config(String)` and `From` impls (`err.to_string()`) collapse source error types.",
          "`crates/temper-agent-runtime/src/tools/mod.rs:11,55` still exposes `anyhow::Result<ToolResult>` in a core trait, which preserves generic-error flow in adjacent runtime code.",
          "`crates/temper-observe/src/error.rs` mixes one typed `#[from] serde_json::Error` variant with multiple `String` variants, reflecting an unfinished conversion to structured error payloads."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Standardize on crate-specific typed errors across runtime/MCP/observe boundaries: replace string payload variants with structured variants carrying source errors (`#[from]` where possible), and migrate `ToolRegistry::execute` away from `anyhow::Result` to a dedicated runtime error enum.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
