    "review::.::holistic::package_organization::observe_namespace_contains_management_mutations::ce632054": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::package_organization::observe_namespace_contains_management_mutations::ce632054",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Management mutations are implemented under `observe` namespace, breaking directory boundary intent.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "package_organization",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/api.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/entities.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`api.rs` documents `/api` as management mutations separated from read-only observe routes, but wires `/api/specs/*`, `/api/wasm/modules/*`, and `/api/evolution/*` to `crate::observe::*` handlers.",
          "`observe/evolution.rs` exports `handle_decide` and other mutation-oriented handlers, while sibling `observe/entities.rs` is read/query focused, creating mixed concerns inside one directory."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Staged reorg plan: 1) create `crates/temper-server/src/manage/` with `specs.rs`, `wasm.rs`, `evolution.rs`; 2) move mutation handlers (`handle_load_*`, `upload/delete_wasm_module`, `handle_decide`, `handle_unmet_intent`, `handle_sentinel_check`) from `observe/*` into `manage/*`; 3) keep `observe/*` only for GET/query/SSE read models; 4) update route imports in `api.rs` to `crate::manage::*`; 5) run `rg \"crate::observe::(specs|wasm|evolution)::handle_\" crates/temper-server/src -n` to verify no mutation handlers remain under observe, then run `cargo check -p temper-server` and `cargo test -p temper-server`.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
