          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/specs.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/agents.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Evolution operations mix `Json<_>`, `Result<Json<_>, StatusCode>`, and `Result<Json<_>, (StatusCode, String)>` in the same module (`crates/temper-server/src/observe/evolution/operations.rs`:168-363).",
          "Specs endpoint uses status-code errors (`crates/temper-server/src/observe/specs.rs`:71-120), while agents endpoints never surface status errors and always return `Json` (`crates/temper-server/src/observe/agents.rs`:81-177).",
          "This creates divergent wire contracts for conceptually similar read/report endpoints under `/observe`."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Define one observe API error envelope and one handler contract pattern (e.g., `Result<Json<T>, ApiError>`), then migrate all observe modules to it so status codes and payload schemas are predictable.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
