      "id": "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::authz_runtime_contract_collapses_to_untyped_strings::8daf5bd5",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Authz APIs expose typed errors and string denials simultaneously",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-authz/src/error.rs",
          "crates/temper-authz/src/engine.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/state/entity_ops.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`AuthzError` defines structured variants, but `authorize` returns `AuthzDecision::Deny(String)` for parse/request/context failures.",
          "`ServerState::authorize` and `authorize_with_context` convert authz outcomes to `Result<(), String>`, losing denial/error taxonomy.",
          "Callers therefore cannot reliably distinguish policy denial vs engine/input failures, forcing brittle string matching/log-only handling."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Unify runtime authz contract around a typed denial/error model (for example `Result<AuthzPermit, AuthzFailure>` with explicit `PolicyDenied` vs `EngineError` kinds) and propagate that type through `entity_ops` and HTTP adapters.",
