        "dimension": "authorization_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/odata/common.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/state/dispatch/actions.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/state/entity_ops.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/entity_actor/actor.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`extract_tenant` falls back to first registered tenant or `TenantId::default()` when header is missing.",
          "Legacy dispatch/read helpers (`dispatch_action`, `get_or_spawn_actor`, `get_entity_state`) route through `TenantId::default()`.",
          "`EntityActor::new`/`with_persistence` initialize tenant as `\"default\"`, relying on later mutation to enforce tenant isolation."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make tenant explicit at request boundaries (reject missing tenant for tenant-scoped APIs), deprecate default-tenant wrappers in server state APIs, and enforce constructor-level tenant binding for entity actors.",
