    "review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::inconsistent-test-file-placement::23aa90b3": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::inconsistent-test-file-placement::23aa90b3",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Test files use two different organizational patterns: some modules use #[cfg(test)] #[path = \"mod_test.rs\"] mod tests (e.g., observe/mod.rs references mod_test.rs), while integration tests live in crates/*/tests/ directories. The lib_tests.rs in temper-mcp uses yet another pattern. This creates navigational friction.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "convention_outlier",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/observe/mod_test.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/src/router_test.rs",
          "crates/temper-mcp/src/lib_tests.rs",
          "crates/temper-server/tests/dst_lifecycle.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "observe/mod.rs uses #[path = \"mod_test.rs\"] for unit tests (1221 LOC)",
          "router.rs tests are in router_test.rs at the same level (675 LOC)",
          "temper-mcp uses lib_tests.rs (927 LOC) for unit tests",
          "Integration tests are properly separated in crates/*/tests/ directories",
          "Some test files are larger than the production files they test"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Standardize on one unit test placement pattern across all crates. The #[path = \"*_test.rs\"] pattern is fine when files are small, but tests that exceed 500 LOC should be split. Consider whether the massive test files (mod_test.rs at 1221 LOC) would be better as integration tests in the tests/ directory.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
