      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "require_policy_auth returns Option<Response> where Some means denied -- inverted semantics",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "naming_quality",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/temper-server/src/api/mod.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "require_policy_auth returns Option<axum::response::Response> where None means authorized and Some(response) means denied",
          "Every call site uses 'if let Some(resp) = require_policy_auth(...) { return resp; }' -- the double-negation pattern (if-some then return) is unusual",
          "The sibling require_observe_auth returns Result<(), StatusCode> which is the standard pattern"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Refactor require_policy_auth to return Result<(), Response> to match the require_observe_auth convention. Callers would use the standard '?' operator instead of the if-let-return pattern.",
